# TypeScript Type Conventions

## Shared Types Location

All shared API/DTO types live in `src/lib/types.ts`. Import as `import type { ... } from "@/lib/types"`.

Domain-specific types co-locate with their helper module (e.g., `BristolCategory` / `BristolInfo` in `@/lib/bristol`). Keep `types.ts` for cross-cutting request/response shapes.

## Naming Conventions

- `*FormData` — data sent from client to API (e.g., `SymptomFormData`)
- `*Response` — data returned from API to client (e.g., `SymptomResponse`)
- `SignificantEvent*` — date/time free-text "fait marquant" payloads and responses
- `ExportData` — full export payload (versioned, `version: 1`)
- `ImportResult` — import operation result with counts

## Adding New Types

When adding a new feature/model:

1. Create `*FormData` interface for the creation payload
2. Create `*Response` interface matching the API JSON output
3. Add the new data to `ExportData` (optional field for backward compat)
4. Update `ExportMetrics` with the count field

## Date Handling

All dates in types are ISO strings (`string`), not `Date` objects. Conversion happens at the API boundary and in display components using `date-fns`.
